@startuml video-source-environment
title R12 video input — environment model (M1, CarSky Room)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

package "Repo (build time)" {
  artifact "ADA_ECU/media/ego-b-occluding-c.mp4\nH.264 / MP4, user-supplied" as CLIP
  artifact "ADA_ECU/Dockerfile\nCOPY media/ -> /app/media/" as DF
}

package "CarSky Room (runtime)" {
  node "ADA ECU (Container Node)" as ADA {
    component "detector subprocess (Python)\nOpenCV VideoCapture -> YOLO11n ONNX CPU" as DET
    component "ADA core (C++17)\nR3 store, R13, R14, R15" as CORE
    file "/app/media/ego-b-occluding-c.mp4" as INFILE
  }
  node "Ethernet Bridge Node" as BR
  node "V2X ECU (Container Node)" as V2X
  node "Bench Scenario Player (Container Node)" as BENCH
}

CLIP --> DF : baked into the image
DF --> INFILE : image layer
INFILE --> DET : VIDEO_CLIP_PATH (env, blueprint node config)
DET --> CORE : R3 TrackedObject JSONL on stdout
BENCH --> BR : ethernet pin (R1 CPM)
BR --> V2X : ethernet pin
V2X --> BR : ethernet pin (R2 JSON)
BR --> ADA : ethernet pin

note right of ADA
  No `video` pin is declared in M1.
  CarSky's `video` pin is an iceoryx2
  shared-memory RGBA transport only —
  the platform publishes no camera or
  dashcam content onto it.
end note

legend bottom
  <b>Legend — every R-number is a requirement ID from the report §2. There is no separate "message" numbering.</b>
  <b>R1–R6</b> are the //contract// requirements: the deliverable //is// a schema or a topology, which is why
  "an R2 message" or "an R3 object" reads like a message name — it is shorthand for the artifact
  that requirement defines. <b>R7–R19</b> are //behavioural// requirements: the deliverable is running code.
  ====
  |= ID |= Kind |= Deliverable |= On this diagram |
  | R1 | contract | ETSI CPM profile (ASN.1 UPER) | bench → V2X ECU over the bridge |
  | R2 | contract | V2X ECU → ADA object message (JSON/UDP) | V2X ECU → ADA ECU |
  | R3 | contract | <b>TrackedObject</b> schema — one shape for every ego object, tagged `own_sensor` or `v2x_relayed` | detector stdout → ADA core |
  | R12 | behaviour | object detection from video | the detector subprocess |
  | R13 | behaviour | track store + admission state machine | inside ADA core |
  | R14 | behaviour | Collision Risk Assessment abstraction | inside ADA core |
  | R15 | behaviour | warning output to the IVI | inside ADA core |
  ====
  <b>CarSky words.</b> **Container Node** = a deployable OCI image · **pin** = a node's typed connection point,
  wired like-to-like only · **`video` pin** = iceoryx2 shared-memory RGBA transport, a pipe with no content
  behind it. <b>ego / B / C.</b> ego = vehicle A, the warned car · B = the visible occluder A's camera detects ·
  C = the occluded car A can never see directly.
endlegend

@enduml
